🔧 Pre-Deployment Checklist (READ BEFORE DEPLOYING)
1. Existing Bucket Pre-Reqs ⚠️

Your fixyachips-platform-980049663300 bucket likely has an existing bucket policy. Before deploying:

# Backup current policy
aws s3api get-bucket-policy --bucket fixyachips-platform-980049663300 \
  --query Policy --output text > backup-policy.json

The CloudFormation deployment will overwrite the existing bucket policy with the OAC-only policy. Make sure that's what you want.
2. Disable any existing Public Access settings on the bucket that might conflict (your screenshots don't show ACLs, but verify "Block all public access" is ON — OAC needs BlockPublicPolicy: false effectively, but the policy I wrote uses aws:SourceArn condition, so all-blocked is fine).
3. SES Sandbox Check

aws ses get-account-sending-enabled --region us-east-1
aws sesv2 get-account --region us-east-1 | grep ProductionAccessEnabled

If in sandbox → request production access before going live, or signups beyond your verified email will silently fail.
4. Route53 Hosted Zone

If you want auto-DNS, pass HostedZoneId parameter. Get it via:

aws route53 list-hosted-zones-by-name --dns-name fixyachips.com

If empty, you'll need to manually create:

    fixyachips.com A-ALIAS → CloudFront
    www.fixyachips.com A-ALIAS → CloudFront

5. Deploy Command

aws cloudformation deploy \
  --template-file fixyachips-v5.1.yaml \
  --stack-name fixyachips-prod \
  --capabilities CAPABILITY_IAM CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --parameter-overrides \
    HostedZoneId=Z0XXXXXXXXXXXX \
    AdminEmail=info@fixyachips.com

6. Post-Deploy

    Confirm SNS subscription email
    Verify SES identity (check info@fixyachips.com inbox)
    Test signup endpoint:

    curl -X POST https://<api-id>.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/prod/signup \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"email":"test@example.com","name":"Test User"}'

